From 73c86e3e3a27683c9cbd09ff4a83e335b77a024e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:00:56 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 18/44] GE: depth test and writes for through-mode draws

Through-mode vertices carry their own depth (z, 0 to 65535), and the GE
tests and writes it as for any transformed draw. The renderer turned the
depth test off for every through-mode draw, which in Vulkan also stops its
depth writes. A game that masks its interface with depth (draws with every
colour bit masked that only write depth, then the visible part depth-tested
against them) lost the mask: a health bar cut to length by a slanted
depth-only quad was drawn full whatever the health.

The shader already maps a through vertex's z to the same [0, 1] device
depth as a transformed one's. <prefix>_NO_THROUGH_DEPTH leaves through-mode
draws untested and unwritten, as before.

Verified on Windows (Vulkan, AMD) with one game: its battle health bars
now shorten with the health and show the drained part, as on the
handheld; title, menus, character select, battle setup, results and
options look as before; no extra depth copies or render passes a frame.
Not verified: other games' 2D screens, which now test depth where they
enable it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 host/gpu/vulkan_renderer.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/host/gpu/vulkan_renderer.cpp b/host/gpu/vulkan_renderer.cpp
index bf26317..1987b13 100644
--- a/host/gpu/vulkan_renderer.cpp
+++ b/host/gpu/vulkan_renderer.cpp
@@ -6867,7 +6867,14 @@ void VulkanRenderer::submit(const DrawCall &call, const GuestMemory &memory) {
             ((call.blend.fixed_source + call.blend.fixed_destination) & 0x00FFFFFFu) == 0x00FFFFFFu)
             key.destination_factor = kFactorInverseConstant;
         key.equation = call.blend.equation;
-        key.depth_test = call.depth.test_enabled && !call.through;
+        // Through-mode vertices carry their own depth (z, 0 to 65535), and the
+        // GE tests and writes it as for any other draw: a game masks parts of
+        // its interface with depth-only draws (every colour bit masked) and then
+        // draws through that mask, which is how a health bar is cut to length.
+        // <prefix>_NO_THROUGH_DEPTH leaves through-mode draws untested and
+        // unwritten, as before.
+        static const bool no_through_depth = portablekit::env("NO_THROUGH_DEPTH") != nullptr;
+        key.depth_test = call.depth.test_enabled && (!call.through || !no_through_depth);
         key.depth_write = call.depth.write_enabled;
         key.depth_function = call.depth.function;
         key.cull = call.culling_enabled && !call.through && call.primitive != PrimitiveType::Sprites;
